# Canonical architecture source. The checked-in SVG is a hand-authored accessible
# fallback because the D2 CLI was unavailable, not a claimed generated render.
direction: down
fsdp: FSDP / ZeRO-3 — shard state, materialize one unit {
  direction: right
  shards: Per-rank parameter + optimizer shards
  gather: All-gather unit weights
  compute: Forward / backward on local examples
  reduce: Reduce-scatter summed gradients
  update: Update owned parameter shard
  shards -> gather
  gather -> compute
  compute -> reduce
  reduce -> update
  update -> shards: next step
}
ring: Context parallel — keep queries local, rotate keys and values {
  direction: right
  r0: Rank 0\nQ positions 0–2\nK/V owner 0
  r1: Rank 1\nQ positions 3–5\nK/V owner 1
  r2: Rank 2\nQ position 6 + 2 pads\nK/V owner 2
  r0 -> r1: K/V block
  r1 -> r2: K/V block
  r2 -> r0: K/V block
}
contract: |md
  **Different groups, different traffic.** FSDP moves model state; context parallelism moves sequence blocks.
  Each query consumes all three K/V owners with one online-softmax state.
  Mask by absolute position and valid length, never by local rank order.
  CPU reference simulates this order: no measured GPU speed or real ring network.
|
fsdp -> ring: complementary techniques; no shared group implied
ring -> contract
